    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d741">

                <pb facs="0692" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/96: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-09T16:00:00+03:06">April 9, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 9—11:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. In note dated today Saudi Government accepted Treasury’s proposal for
                    conversion dollars into rials described first paragraph Department’s unnumbered
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">45?</hi>] March 23, 9 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >7?</hi>] p.m.</p>
                <p>Last 7 million Lend-Lease rials arrived Jidda March 6 and delivered to Saudi
                    Government immediately. Probably most have been spent already. In reply
                    suggestion that Saudi Government begin sale rials under conversion plan price
                    receipt of 10 million new Lend-Lease rials both Finance Minister and Acting
                    Foreign Minister expressed willingness do so within limitations of Government’s
                    financial resources.</p>
                <p>Acting Foreign Minister confirmed that Saudi Government cannot accept interest
                    payments (my 81, March 27, noon<anchor n="59" xml:id="d741-f1"/>) and therefore
                    suggested that deposit with Federal Reserve Bank be utilized as revolving fund
                    for conversion dollars to rials by some procedure to be agreed on later. This
                    suggestion was not a condition of acceptance of Treasury’s plan.</p>
                <p>Please advise immediately details procedure to put plan into effect.</p>
                <p>When new rials are shipped Saudi Government wishes delivery of 1 million rials at
                    Jidda and 9 million via Bahrein or if that is impracticable, delivery of entire
                    number through Bahrein.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d741-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d741-f1" n="59" xml:id="d741-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d741-f2" n="60" xml:id="d741-f2-content">
                <p>In his telegram 250, August 14, 7 p.m., the Minister Resident advised that the
                    Saudi Arabian Government preferred to receive all 10 million riyals at the Saudi
                    Arabian port of Ras Tanura (890 F.515/8–1444).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
